# EXPECT_COMPILE_ERROR: bad_select_subject_bool_chain.obs:(11,11): Expected integer or string expression
# EXPECT_ERROR_COUNT: 1
#~
The subject of a 'select' is typed by its value, the end of its call chain: a chain that starts
with a String and ends in a Bool is neither an integer nor a string. It was typed by its head, so
this was taken for a select on a string and refused twice, by errors about something else
("Undefined function/method call: 'HashID(..)'", "Integer label in a select on a string").
~#
class BadSelectSubjectBoolChain {
	function : Main(args : String[]) ~ Nil {
		select("ab"->Equals(args[0])) {
			label 1 {
				"equal"->PrintLine();
			}
			other {
				"other"->PrintLine();
			}
		};
	}
}
